---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<Base
  title="cairn — a roadmap that lives in your repository"
  description="cairn keeps a project's roadmap and issues as Markdown files in the repository, under a schema you define, with tools that let coding agents work the backlog."
  wide
>
  <!-- The artefact is the argument: an item is a file, so show the file. -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__claim">
        <h1>Your backlog is a directory of Markdown files.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          cairn keeps a project's roadmap and issues in the repository itself,
          under a schema you declare. Reviewable in the pull request that closes
          them. Readable in ten years. No server, no account, no browser.
        </p>

        <div class="install">
          <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oddurs/cairn/main/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
          <p class="install__alt">
            Or <code>brew tap oddurs/cairn &amp;&amp; brew install cairn</code>.
            Linux, macOS and Windows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="hero__links">
          <a class="cta" href={`${base}/docs`}>Read the docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/oddurs/cairn">Source on GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero__file slab">
        <figcaption>cairn/items/0001-support-oauth-login.md</figcaption>
        <pre><code><span class="d">---</span>
<span class="b">id</span>: 1
<span class="b">title</span>: Support OAuth login
<span class="b">type</span>: feature
<span class="b">status</span>: doing
<span class="b">milestone</span>: v0.1
<span class="b">priority</span>: p0
<span class="d">---</span>

<span class="k">## Problem</span>

Password auth is the only option, and
enterprise users keep asking for SSO.

<span class="k">## Acceptance criteria</span>

- [ ] Authorization code flow with PKCE
- [ ] Refresh tokens survive a restart</code></pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Recorded from real command output, so it cannot drift into flattery. -->
  <section class="band band--deep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What using it looks like</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every frame below is real output, recorded by running the commands. It
        is regenerated on every change, and continuous integration fails if it
        no longer matches.
      </p>
      <img
        class="demo"
        src={`${base}/demo.svg`}
        alt="A terminal session: creating two items where the second depends on the first, running cairn next, claiming the top item, closing it, and watching the dependent item become available."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <p class="note">
        Note the third command. <code>0002</code> depends on <code>0001</code>,
        so it stays off the list until <code>0001</code> closes.
        <code>cairn next</code> shows work that is genuinely startable, not everything
        that is open.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Strata rather than three identical cards: each idea is a full band with
       its own weight, separated by hairlines. -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap strata">
      <article class="stratum">
        <h3>The schema is yours</h3>
        <div class="stratum__body">
          <p>
            Item types, statuses, custom fields, milestones and saved views are
            declared in one file. Rename <code>doing</code> to
            <code>on the pass</code> if that is what your team says — every
            status belongs to a fixed category, so progress bars and
            <code>cairn close</code> keep working whatever you call things.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="stratum__code slab"><code><span class="d">[[status]]</span>
<span class="b">name</span> = "doing"
<span class="b">label</span> = "in progress"
<span class="b">category</span> = "active"
<span class="b">color</span> = "yellow"</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="stratum">
        <h3>Agents work the backlog</h3>
        <div class="stratum__body">
          <p>
            <code>cairn mcp</code> serves the backlog over the Model Context
            Protocol. An agent gets typed tools rather than instructions it can
            forget, and a rejected write comes back as something it can act on.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="stratum__code slab"><code>update_item <span class="d">&#123;"status": "in progress"&#125;</span>

<span class="r">unknown status `in progress`</span>
<span class="d">known: backlog, planned, doing,
       blocked, done, dropped</span></code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="stratum">
        <h3>Nothing drifts</h3>
        <div class="stratum__body">
          <p>
            <code>ROADMAP.md</code> is generated, and re-rendered whenever an
            item changes. <code>cairn check</code> validates every item against
            the schema and proves the committed roadmap still matches, which is
            one line in continuous integration.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="stratum__code slab"><code>$ cairn check
<span class="r">cairn</span>: <span class="d">items/0009-bad.md:4:</span>
  unknown status `nope`

<span class="r">failed</span>: 1 error across 4 items</code></pre>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--deep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Built to be left alone</h2>
      <div class="pairs">
        <div>
          <h3>Writes cannot be half-finished</h3>
          <p>
            Every file is written beside its target, flushed, and renamed over
            it. A crash leaves the old contents or the new ones, never a
            mixture. There is a test that kills the program mid-write forty
            times.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Branches merge without a fight</h3>
          <p>
            Two branches that both add an item would conflict in the generated
            roadmap and collide on an identifier. Neither is a real conflict, so
            <code>cairn init --git</code> teaches git to re-derive both instead.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>The format is specified</h3>
          <p>
            The item format is <a href={`${base}/format`}>written down</a>
            independently of this program, versioned, and pinned by a corpus of
            files that must keep parsing the same way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Concurrent writers are safe</h3>
          <p>
            Mutating commands take a lock; reads never do. Forty processes
            creating items at once produce forty distinct identifiers, and
            twelve agents racing for one item produce exactly one owner.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band close">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start in one command</h2>
      <pre class="slab"><code>$ cairn init
<span class="g">created</span> cairn.toml
<span class="g">created</span> cairn/items/

$ cairn new <span class="y">"Support OAuth login"</span> --type feature --milestone v0.1
<span class="g">created</span> 0001  Support OAuth login</code></pre>
      <p class="hero__links">
        <a class="cta" href={`${base}/docs`}>Read the docs</a>
        <a href={`${base}/docs/agents`}>Set it up for an agent</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero {
      padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
    }
    .hero__inner {
      display: grid;
      gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
    @media (min-width: 62rem) {
      .hero__inner {
        grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
      }
    }
    .hero__claim h1 {
      margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    }
    .hero__claim .lede {
      max-width: 44ch;
    }

    .install {
      margin-block: 1.75rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .install pre {
      background: var(--slate-deep);
      border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
      border-left: 2px solid var(--lichen);
      border-radius: 3px;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
    }
    .install__alt {
      margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
      color: var(--moss);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }
    .install__alt code {
      color: var(--chalk);
      font-size: 0.85em;
    }

    .hero__links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.75rem;
    }
    .cta {
      background: var(--lichen);
      color: var(--slate);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .cta:hover {
      background: #c8d84f;
    }

    .hero__file figcaption {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--moss);
      padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
      background: var(--slate);
    }

    .demo {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      margin-block: 2rem 1.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .note {
      color: var(--moss);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      max-width: 62ch;
    }

    .strata {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .stratum {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.25rem 3rem;
      padding-block: 2.25rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
      align-items: start;
    }
    .stratum:first-child {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
    .stratum:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }
    @media (min-width: 54rem) {
      .stratum {
        grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 20rem);
      }
    }
    .stratum h3 {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--chalk);
    }
    .stratum__body p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--moss);
    }
    .stratum__code {
      font-size: 0.78rem;
    }

    .pairs {
      display: grid;
      gap: 2rem 3.5rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    @media (min-width: 46rem) {
      .pairs {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }
    .pairs h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .pairs p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--moss);
    }

    .close pre {
      max-width: 52rem;
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }
    .close h2 {
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
